course: dictionary
lesson: 14997
title: Reputable: trusted and good
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reputable is an adjective. It describes someone or something that is known to be honest, reliable and good. Reputation means what people generally think about a person or thing, so a reputable source has a good reputation.
explain: «Ella checked a reputable website before she copied facts for her project.» Checking and copying facts tells you that Ella wanted trustworthy information. Reputable must mean a website people can trust.
explain: «Dad bought our puppy from a reputable breeder, not from a stranger online.» The word stranger is the clue. A stranger is someone you do not know, so a reputable breeder is one people know and trust.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simpler word such as trusted or good. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. «Dad bought our puppy from a trusted breeder» works, so you are right.
fact: Reputable means known to be honest, reliable and good.
fact: A reputation is what people generally think about someone or something.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «a reputable company» and «a reputable source».
fact: Choosing a reputable website, breeder or builder helps keep you safe and get good results.
exercise: «Mum hired a reputable builder to fix the roof.» What does reputable mean here? | *Known to be honest and good at the job | Painted bright red | New and never used before | Known for being very loud
exercise: Which source is most reputable for a school project? | *An encyclopedia from a well-known publisher | A post by someone you have never heard of | A joke video with no facts | A website nobody has ever heard of
exercise: Dad says «a reputable breeder» is one people trust. What does reputable mean? | Hard to find in shops | Hungry for food | *Trusted and known to be good | Pretty and colourful
test: «The shop has a reputable name, so people buy from it every day.» What does reputable mean? | Very big and very old | Closed on Sundays | Loud and busy | *Trusted and good
test: Which is the best choice when buying a bike? | A bike with no wheels | A cheap bike from a stranger online | A bike from a shop nobody knows | *A bike from a reputable shop with good reviews
exam: Jayden wants a safe website for his homework. Which should he choose? | A site with no name or contact details | A pop-up site that promises free prizes | *A website from a reputable school library | A site his friend made up for fun
